<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Predicting school arrival times using weather-dependent tree diagrams</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The probability that it rains on a school day in Nairobi is <b>{@str_R@}</b>. If it rains, the probability that Atieno arrives late for school is <b>{@str_LR@}</b>. If it does not rain, the probability she is late is <b>{@str_LNR@}</b>.</p>

<p>Draw a two-stage tree diagram for this scenario and use it to solve the following questions:</p>

<p><b>a) </b> Find the probability that Atieno is late for school.</p>
<p><i>(Enter your answer as an exact decimal).</i></p>
<p>\(P =\) [[input:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>

<p><b>b) </b> Find the probability that it rained, but she was <b>NOT</b> late.</p>
<p>\(P =\) [[input:ans2]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p>First, establish the probabilities for all branches on the tree diagram:</p>
<ul>
  <li>\(P(\text{Rain}) = {@str_R@}\) $\Rightarrow$ \(P(\text{No Rain}) = 1 - {@str_R@} = {@str_NR@}\)</li>
  <li>\(P(\text{Late} \mid \text{Rain}) = {@str_LR@}\) $\Rightarrow$ \(P(\text{Not Late} \mid \text{Rain}) = 1 - {@str_LR@} = {@str_LNR_given_R@}\)</li>
  <li>\(P(\text{Late} \mid \text{No Rain}) = {@str_LNR@}\) $\Rightarrow$ \(P(\text{Not Late} \mid \text{No Rain}) = 1 - {@str_LNR@} = {@str_NL_given_NR@}\)</li>
</ul>

<p><b>Part a: Probability she is Late</b><br>
The event "Atieno is late" corresponds to two paths on the tree diagram: (Rain $\rightarrow$ Late) and (No Rain $\rightarrow$ Late).</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(\text{Rain, Late}) = {@str_R@} \times {@str_LR@} = {@path_R_L@} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(\text{No Rain, Late}) = {@str_NR@} \times {@str_LNR@} = {@path_NR_L@} \)</p>
<p>Add these path probabilities together:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(\text{Late}) = {@path_R_L@} + {@path_NR_L@} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ P(\text{Late}) = {@ta1_str@} } \)</p>

<p><b>Part b: Rain and Not Late</b><br>
This corresponds to a single path on the tree diagram: (Rain $\rightarrow$ Not Late).</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(\text{Rain, Not Late}) = P(\text{Rain}) \times P(\text{Not Late} \mid \text{Rain}) \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(\text{Rain, Not Late}) = {@str_R@} \times {@str_LNR_given_R@} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ P(\text{Rain, Not Late}) = {@ta2_str@} } \)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
